 ## Type Scale
 
-| Surface | Standard |
-|---|---|
-| User and assistant message containers | `text-ui-lg` |
-| Markdown body | `text-ui-base` |
-| h1 | `text-ui-xl` (`--ui-font-size + 4px`) |
-| h2 | `text-ui-lg` (`--ui-font-size + 2px`) |
-| h3 | `text-ui-base` |
-| h4-h6 | `text-ui-base` |
-| Normal and file links | `text-ui-base` |
-| Inline code | `font-mono text-ui-sm` |
-| Code block body | default `14px` |
-| Code block header | `text-ui-base` |
-| Tables | `text-ui-base` |
+| Surface                               | Standard                              |
+| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
+| User and assistant message containers | `text-ui-lg`                          |
+| Markdown body                         | `text-ui-base`                        |
+| h1                                    | `text-ui-xl` (`--ui-font-size + 4px`) |
+| h2                                    | `text-ui-lg` (`--ui-font-size + 2px`) |
+| h3                                    | `text-ui-base`                        |
+| h4-h6                                 | `text-ui-base`                        |
+| Normal and file links                 | `text-ui-base`                        |
+| Inline code                           | `font-mono text-ui-sm`                |
+| Code block body                       | default `14px`                        |
+| Code block header                     | `text-ui-base`                        |
+| Tables                                | `text-ui-base`                        |
+
+## Spacing
+
+Assistant Markdown uses a reading rhythm that is tighter than a document layout while still separating blocks:
+
+| Element                  | Spacing                                        |
+| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |
+| Between top-level blocks | `12px` (`space-y-3`)                           |
+| Body line height         | `1.65`                                         |
+| Body letter spacing      | font default (no `tracking-wide`)              |
+| `h1`-`h6`                | `mt-4 mb-2`                                    |
+| Lists                    | `my-2`; items `space-y-1`; nested lists `my-1` |
+| Code block, blockquote   | `my-3`                                         |
+
+- Block separation is owned solely by the Markdown root's `space-y-*`; paragraphs carry no vertical margin of their own, so the two rhythms cannot stack.
+- Body text keeps the font's default letter spacing. `tracking-wide` widens every glyph, and CJK paragraphs read noticeably looser because of it; readability is carried by the line height instead.
+- The first and last blocks stay flush with the container (`[&>*:first-child]:mt-0`, `[&>*:last-child]:mb-0`). The action footer's `mt-1` remains the only gap between body text and the toolbar.
+- Desktop and remote-control mobile share this density; narrow viewports are not compressed further, so body text never touches the edges.
 
