+# Compact result details
+
+## Scope
+
+Extend the existing V4 compact timeline marker; do not create another transcript message. Manual compact stays in the timeline-only lane and automatic compact stays in assistant work. Summary messages remain hidden from transcript, model history is not duplicated, and default sharing/export does not acquire summary bodies. Compaction prompts, profiles, preservation/tail policy and model requests are unchanged.
+
+## Presentation
+
+- Every marker names its origin (automatic/manual) and lifecycle (running/completed/no-op/failed/cancelled/interrupted). Only durable successful results have expandable details.
+- Successful markers default to collapsed, intentionally unlike OpenCode's immediately expanded summary, to avoid long summaries taking over the conversation.
+- The title shows estimated context tokens before and after. Both are local context estimates: `preCompactTokenCount` and **only** `truePostCompactTokenCount`. `postCompactTokenCount` is summary-request usage, never post-compaction context size. Missing historical counts display unknown, not zero or usage. Format finite nonnegative estimates as integer numbers with `Intl.NumberFormat` and the current locale; the existing lightweight `IntlInstance` only supplies message formatting and must not be expanded for this view.
+- Expanding loads the saved Markdown from `MessageInfo.summary.body`; never display early `ModelComplete.content`, reconstruct from visible messages, or call a model again. Use the shared Markdown renderer, semantic colors and `text-ui-*` typography. Collapsing hides the details. Loading, unavailable and read-error states are distinct and localized in Chinese/English.
+- Old records lacking the reference, durable boundary or body display an explicit unavailable explanation. Failed/running/no-op/cancelled/interrupted markers cannot claim to have a summary.
+
+## Read boundary
+
+Add `v4/conversation/compactSummary` on the existing workspace-owned service/transport/gateway path. Request carries session, log epoch, branch generation, marker row, operation and summary reference. The active projection must contain that exact successful marker. A missing/mismatched row, operation or reference is not authorized; stale log/branch identity is explicitly unavailable. Repeat authorization after asynchronous storage reads.
+
+The CLI bridge uses the existing session store's `getSession` and session-scoped `messageWithParts` to fetch **one** summary. It does not load the entire transcript for one summary. Verify session identity, current durable branch generation, hidden `compact_summary` semantics and the matching durable compaction part's operation and boundary `summaryMessageIds`. Active-branch membership comes from the authoritative projected marker, built by the existing branch-aware cold hydration; a stored arbitrary message ID is never sufficient. Cold recovery only restores a reference when the active transcript contains that trusted hidden summary's own session/message/operation-matching compaction boundary. A surviving timeline carrier, even one containing a copied boundary, cannot prove ownership of a retired summary. Preserve earlier carrier routing metadata such as source command and anchor while the persisted boundary supplies final status, reference and true estimates. Unsupported/legacy records degrade to unavailable. Bound summary size to keep the ordinary RPC envelope below 1 MiB; oversized content is unavailable, never silently truncated into a different summary.
+
+Cold merge owns the distinction between historical and still-live compaction. Transcript-only `started`/`retrying` facts recover as interrupted. At first materialization, a same-session, same-operation latest live `CompactStarted` (`started`/`retrying`) remains active if its turn has not ended and no later compact terminal or session-resume boundary retired it. For an existing carrier, its durable message and part must also match. Replace the provisional interruption synthesized from that in-flight carrier with this trusted live fact after replaying completed transcript turns, preserving the running marker, compact active work, operation lock and Stop affordance. Never treat a different operation/session or a historical start followed by a terminal as proof of liveness. Durable completed summary/boundary facts always take precedence over stale live starts.
+
+No direct renderer/host database access, new authentication flow, approval bypass, writes, credentials or automatic export/share inclusion.
+
+## Identity and races
+
+Expose additive branch generation with snapshots/state updates and restore it from the existing durable session revert metadata. A committed conversation rewind updates it even when the target row is outside the loaded projection. UI request state is isolated by workspace identity/path, session, log epoch, branch generation, row, operation and summary reference; changing any identity resets expansion and content. Do not install a global summary cache. Effect cleanup ignores late fulfilled/rejected responses; stale data and errors never render in a reused row or another session. Server rechecks projected and durable identity after I/O.
+
+## Deferred validation (not run during implementation)
+
+- Shared schemas: strict bounded request/result identities; invalid/missing/cross-scope fields rejected.
+- Gateway/bridge: one scoped read; durable body and operation checks; old/missing/oversized body; non-success statuses; arbitrary ID/session/operation/ref; stale log/branch; branch change while a read is pending; cold restoration.
+- Projection: same marker upsert through lifecycle; use only true post estimate; legacy usage-only remains unknown; committed rewind generation is propagated and cold seeded.
+- UI: collapsed by default; one lazy fetch per opening; Markdown; unknown tokens; localized origin/status/error/unavailable; collapse; row/session/workspace/branch/ref identity changes and late success/error ignored.
+- Unified interactive acceptance: manual/automatic layout, expansion/collapse and keyboard access; restart then expand the same durable summary; legacy missing body; stop/failure/no-op/interruption; rewind while expanded; narrow/wide Zai Light/Dark. Run existing compact desktop E2E plus the focused component tests after both development lines stop writing.
