+# Context source update notices
+
+## Scope
+
+Project the dynamic resource core's persisted `ContextSourceUpdate` v1 metadata as an audit notice in the existing V4 timeline. This is a source catalog change receipt, not a user message, permission grant, tool invocation or full system-prompt viewer.
+
+Trusted metadata includes version, kind (`skills`, `agents`, `mcp_tools`, or `instructions`), aggregate source key, revision and item changes (`added`, `replaced`, `removed`, source key and display label). Project only these explicitly allowlisted fields. Never display hidden text-part content, loaded Skill body, Agent system prompt, MCP credentials or runtime checkpoint metadata. Old hidden messages without valid metadata stay hidden. No model call or history duplication.
+
+## Live and restored facts
+
+The existing `persistPart` path has no SessionEvent notification, only a logger event. The core line must publish a sanitized `SystemMessage` subtype `context_source_update` after durable part persistence, carrying message ID, part ID and `sourceUpdate`, with content limited to safe change labels (or empty). Bootstrap ignores that content. Cold hydration reads the same top-level part metadata (or runtimeMessage.sourceUpdate compatibility field) on a trusted agent-runtime hidden synthetic message from `context_source_update`, `instruction_file_update`, `agent_listing_delta` or `tool_search_announcement` and synthesizes the same event. Identity is the durable part ID; live/cold deduplicate it and never create two notices for the same part. Branch-aware cold materialization excludes retired notices. Memory-only notice facts require an exact message ID still present in the active transcript, even when that transcript is empty; without durable branch proof cold recovery fails closed. Malformed or over-limit metadata is not projected; no silent body or list truncation is performed.
+
+## UI
+
+Use an additive `timelineMarker` variant, leaving snapshot state unchanged. The notice names the source category and counts additions/replacements/removals. Render only safe item labels with localized change verbs. Keep the view dense; small lists are visible, long lists are collapsed behind an accessible native details control to avoid flooding a long session. There is no hidden-body expander. Chinese and English copy use the existing locale files and design tokens. Default sharing keeps omitting runtime marker rows; the lower-level public projection explicitly rejects source-update notices rather than publishing catalog keys or paths. No new export or shared-context inclusion is added.
+
+## Deferred validation
+
+Write shared schema, pure projection/hydration and component coverage before implementation. Cover valid live/cold metadata, same-part deduplication, all source/change categories, malformed/untrusted/legacy metadata, absence of hidden prompt text in serialized rows, and long-list collapse. Do not run tests, typecheck, Lint, format checks, architecture checks or preview during parallel implementation. Main agent runs unified acceptance after both writers stop.
