@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Status capsule compacts while the side pane is open
+
+## Context
+
+The conversation status capsule (the collapsed `StatusSummaryRow` inside
+`ConversationStatusPanel`) sits at the conversation's top-right corner. When the
+right Side Pane is open, that corner is crowded and the capsule can overlap the
+side-pane frame on narrow containers.
+
+## Trigger
+
+The capsule compacts only while the right Side Pane is open.
+
+- Single owner: `useAppPanels.isSidePaneCollapsed` -> `App.isSidePaneOpen`.
+- The layout module already receives that value as `isSidePaneOpen`; it passes it
+  into both main conversation trees. Do not derive a second copy, and do not use
+  the `isSidePaneVisible` animation state.
+- Opening the bottom terminal must not compact the capsule.
+
+## Behavior
+
+- When the side pane opens, the capsule automatically shrinks to an icon-only
+  control: roughly a 32px square (`h-8`, `w-8`), no horizontal content padding,
+  no gap, icon centered.
+- The full summary content (label, counts, Git `+added` / `-removed`, workflow
+  phase, and so on) is visually clipped in compact mode, but remains in the DOM
+  through `sr-only` so screen readers and the accessible tree keep the summary
+  semantics.
+- When the side pane closes, the capsule restores exactly the summary it showed
+  before (the same branch priority and the same content), with its original
+  width/padding.
+- Repeated open/close cycles are idempotent; the compact state is a pure
+  projection of `isSidePaneOpen`.
+- The capsule is never hidden. It stays clickable and keeps its accessible name
+  (`chat.summaryPanel.showPanel`) and hover hint in compact mode.
+- Hover and focus still swap the status icon for the maximize affordance, as in
+  the current full capsule.
+- Padding/gap changes transition with the existing low-drama timing, and
+  `prefers-reduced-motion` disables that transition.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Do not change the user's `summaryPanelVariantOverride` (`panel` / `mini`).
+- Do not force an expanded status panel to collapse; the trigger applies only to
+  the capsule entry point. When the user has pinned the panel open, it stays
+  open.
+- Do not apply the compact treatment to the Side Pane tree or side chat.
+- Do not trigger from terminal visibility, window width, or any other signal.
+
+## Implementation contract
+
+New managed module `packages/ui/src/v4/status-capsule/`:
+
+- `contract.ts` is the leaf props contract (`SidePaneCapsuleScopeProps`,
+  `StatusCapsuleMetricProps`); it imports only React types.
+- `StatusCapsuleContext.ts` exposes the boolean compact context and
+  `useStatusCapsuleCompact()`. It projects the existing shell state without
+  creating another state owner or synchronization effect.
+- `StatusCapsuleScope.tsx` projects the `compact` prop into that context.
+- `StatusCapsuleButton.tsx` forwards the tooltip trigger ref and attributes,
+  merging its description with a unique reference to the existing full summary
+  content. Screen readers can read Git counts even with an explicit button label.
+- `StatusCapsuleMetric.tsx` owns all compact layout rules. It keeps the original
+  icon slot untouched, wraps the children once, and exposes stable slots:
+  `data-status-capsule`, `data-status-capsule-compact`,
+  `data-status-capsule-icon`, `data-status-capsule-content`. Structural CSS must
+  target these slots, never fragile `:first-child` selectors.
+- `index.ts` is the public entry point, including
+  `withSidePaneCapsuleScope(Component)`.
+
+Integration points:
+
+- `WorkspaceShellLayout.tsx` wraps exactly the two main conversation trees
+  (`V4ChatPane`, `V4WorkspaceChatArea`) with the stable module-level HOC and
+  passes `sidePaneOpen={isSidePaneOpen}`. The HOC is created once at module
+  scope; do not create components during render (that would remount sessions).
+- `ConversationStatusPanel.tsx` keeps one `StatusSummaryMetric` wrapper that
+  delegates to `StatusCapsuleMetric`; individual summary branches must not carry
+  compact conditionals.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Unit/regression (`packages/ui/test/v4StatusCapsuleSidePane.test.ts`):
+  default is not compact; open/close/repeated toggles; provider scope isolation;
+  todo/Git summary semantics preserved under `sr-only`; the capsule click still
+  calls `onVariantChange("panel")`; a pinned panel is not collapsed.
+- Browser fixture/test
+  (`packages/ui/test/browser/manual-review/pending/status-capsule-side-pane.*`):
+  real measured capsule open/close/reopen sizes and content in mini and
+  auto-narrow containers, mouse and keyboard expand, light and dark Zai themes,
+  and narrow viewports.
